    "lawCode": "Rpld §925-t, Gen Muni L",
    "lawSection": "General Municipal",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S368\n\nSPONSOR: GALLIVAN\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to repeal section 925-t of the general municipal law, relating to\nthe town of Concord industrial development agency\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis legislation will effectuate the delisting of the Town of Concord\nIndustrial Development Agency from the New York State Comptroller's list\nof active public authorities.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 of the bill repeals section 925-t of the General Municipal\nlaw. Section 2 establishes the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe Town of Concord, situated within Erie County, has requested this\nlegislation to remove language from New York Statute, which established\nthe Town of Concord Industrial Development Agency (IDA), as a result of\nsuch IDA having no assets and no funds and that it has terminated all\nits legal obligations, bonds, notes and straight-lease transactions and,\nby Town resolution, was deemed to have ceased existence on July 13,\n2022.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately.\n",
    "multiSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
